### Option B: Market Ecosystem & Technology Selection Schema (`reponix/market-research.md`)

```markdown
# Market & Technology Ecosystem Research: {{projectName}}
<!-- Scope: Greenfield Ideation / Architecture Benchmark -->

## 1. Domain & Competitor Landscape
- **Domain / Vertical:** <e.g., Real-Time Ride Hailing & Dispatch, On-Demand Delivery>
- **Market Reference Leaders:** <e.g., Uber, Ola, Lyft, Grab>
- **Core Market Use Cases:**
  1. Real-time driver location ingestion & geospatial indexing (< 1s latency).
  2. High-throughput ride request & multi-factor driver matching.
  3. Dynamic surge pricing engine with geospatial demand aggregation.
  4. Distributed trip state machine with zero-double-dispatch guarantee.

## 2. Industry-Standard Technology Matrix
| Capability | Market Standard Tech | Leading Adopters | Why It Is Chosen | Trade-offs & Alternatives |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Geospatial Indexing | Uber H3 / Google S2 | Uber, Ola | Hexagonal hierarchical spatial cells; constant-time neighbor lookups | R-Trees (higher write overhead at scale) |
| High-Write Ingestion | Apache Kafka / Redpanda | Uber, Netflix, LinkedIn | High-throughput partitioned event streaming, replayable log | RabbitMQ (lower throughput under millions/sec pings) |
| In-Memory Geospatial & Locks | Redis Cluster (GEO, Redlock) | Uber, DoorDash | Sub-millisecond latency, atomic distributed mutex (`SET NX EX`) | Memcached (no geospatial or Lua scripting) |
| Primary Persistence | PostgreSQL + PostGIS / ScyllaDB | Uber (Schemaless/MySQL), Ola | Acid transactions for billing, PostGIS for boundary polygons | MongoDB (trade-offs in complex multi-entity transactions) |
| Service Communication | gRPC / Protocol Buffers | Uber, Netflix, Google | Binary serialization, bidirectional streaming, low CPU overhead | REST/JSON (higher latency and serialization overhead) |

## 3. Recommended Production Stack for Greenfield Implementation
- **Runtime & Language:** <e.g., Go / TypeScript (Node.js/Bun) / Java (Spring Boot)>
- **API & RPC Gateway:** <e.g., Envoy + gRPC / Fastify REST Gateway>
- **Data Tier:** <e.g., PostgreSQL (Transactional) + Redis Cluster (Cache & Spatial) + ScyllaDB (Audit/Trip logs)>
- **Streaming & Messaging:** <e.g., Apache Kafka with Schema Registry>
- **Orchestration:** <e.g., Kubernetes + Helm + Docker multi-stage builds>
```

